 {
  "id": "288c8f99-1c14-4153-8a2e-232dc58ca4f0",
  "organisation_id": null,
  "title": "Splose Induction",
  "description": "The Splose induction for Opal practitioners: account setup, booking, appointment management, progress notes and AI documentation, the Microsoft 365 connection, performance — closed out by a knowledge check and the first-day checklist.",
  "category": "induction",
  "status": "active",
  "draft_content": {
   "sections": [
    {
     "key": "s-80dfcb64",
     "items": [
      {
       "key": "i-1b4d9349",
       "body": "The three systems Opal runs on, what belongs in each, and the one rule that keeps them honest.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Splose at Opal: The Big Picture",
       "minutes": 6,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-at-opal"
      },
      {
       "key": "i-521b8795",
       "body": "Your practitioner profile, the locations and services attached to it, and why a missing service is never solved by picking a different one.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Set Up Your Splose Account",
       "minutes": 10,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-account-setup"
      },
      {
       "key": "i-a2bcfdf6",
       "body": "The Splose calendar, the three booking types, completing a booking properly, and how practitioner–client access really works.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Book a Client Appointment",
       "minutes": 12,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-booking"
      },
      {
       "key": "i-fb96583c",
       "body": "Moving appointments safely, recording cancellations and no-shows through Status, and why Archive is never a cancellation.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Reschedule, Cancel and Status",
       "minutes": 10,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-appointments"
      },
      {
       "key": "i-fe50ee4f",
       "body": "Progress notes from the appointment, structuring a defensible clinical note, and using Splose’s AI drafting without ever letting it write the record for you.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Document the Session",
       "minutes": 15,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-progress-notes"
      },
      {
       "key": "i-708009e0",
       "body": "Your personal Teams connection, telehealth links, the one-way calendar feed into Outlook, and the private URL you must never share.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Connect Splose to Microsoft 365",
       "minutes": 12,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-teams-outlook"
      }
     ],
     "title": "Splose walkthroughs"
    },
    {
     "key": "s-d2b3d61a",
     "items": [
      {
       "key": "i-bb280baf",
       "body": "Reading your own Splose performance report: utilisation, what the numbers do and do not mean, and why incomplete notes come first.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Your Performance Report",
       "minutes": 8,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-performance"
      },
      {
       "key": "i-3b6ded0b",
       "body": "The capstone: a full day across Splose, Outlook and the Opal Portal, the decision drill, and the first-day checklist.\n\nOpen the walkthrough below — your place in it is saved as you go.",
       "type": "task",
       "title": "Your Splose Workflow at Opal",
       "minutes": 12,
       "required": true,
       "walkthrough_key": "splose-daily-workflow"
      }
     ],
     "title": "Splose walkthroughs (continued)"
    },
    {
     "key": "s-fe52f09a",
     "items": [
      {
       "key": "i-bfdaa4d5",
       "body": "Ten questions across the whole Splose induction. The pass mark is 80% — you can retry as often as you need.",
       "quiz": {
        "questions": [
         {
          "options": [
           "In Splose",
           "In the subscribed Outlook calendar",
           "Wherever is quickest"
          ],
          "question": "A participant asks to move tomorrow’s appointment to a new time. Where is the appointment moved?",
          "correctIndex": 0
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "Select a similar service so the booking goes through",
           "Check the selected location and your practitioner service assignment, then escalate to admin if needed",
           "Book it as busy time and fix it later"
          ],
          "question": "A service is missing from your booking screen. What do you do?",
          "correctIndex": 1
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "Appointment",
           "Support activity",
           "Busy time"
          ],
          "question": "Which booking type is used for a normal therapy session?",
          "correctIndex": 0
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "A support activity linked to the client",
           "Emailing the client",
           "Opening the waitlist"
          ],
          "question": "What can create the practitioner–client link before the first appointment?",
          "correctIndex": 0
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "Yes — archive keeps the calendar tidy",
           "No — the status records the cancellation and the history is preserved"
          ],
          "question": "Should a cancelled appointment normally be archived?",
          "correctIndex": 1
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "Cancelled",
           "Did not arrive",
           "No status"
          ],
          "question": "A participant was expected, never attended, and had not cancelled. Which status fits?",
          "correctIndex": 1
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "True",
           "False — every AI draft is verified against the session before finalising"
          ],
          "question": "True or false: AI-generated note text can be saved as long as it reads professionally.",
          "correctIndex": 1
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "Yes",
           "No — Splose publishes to Outlook and nothing flows back"
          ],
          "question": "Is the Splose-to-Outlook calendar feed two-way?",
          "correctIndex": 1
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "Your private Splose calendar-feed URL",
           "Your practitioner column colour",
           "The clinic street address"
          ],
          "question": "What must never be shared with anyone?",
          "correctIndex": 0
         },
         {
          "options": [
           "40%",
           "70%",
           "82%"
          ],
          "question": "Available time 40 hours; arrived appointment time 28 hours. Appointment utilisation?",
          "correctIndex": 1
         }
        ],
        "passThreshold": 80
       },
       "type": "quiz",
       "title": "Splose knowledge check",
       "minutes": 5,
       "required": true
      }
     ],
     "title": "Make it formal"
    }
   ]
  },
